#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""touchbar-strip - a status strip renderer for the T1 Touch Bar (MacBook Pro 2016-2017).

Speaks t1bridge's Touch Bar hardware IPC v1 (t1bridge docs/interfaces.md) and is selected as the
renderer by linking ~/.config/t1bridge/renderer at this file. If it exits, t1bridge's launcher
falls back to the built-in renderer once, so a crash never leaves the bar dead.

Layout, 2170x60:  Esc | clock | agent (a coding agent's state, task and last step) |
                  [task progress] | machine | screen, keyboard, volume dials | lock key
Fn held:          Esc | F1 .. F12          (same 13 slots as the stock bar)
Lock screen:      a black bar and the fingerprint key (no Cancel, never a new verify)

Everything a slot does on tap or hold comes from ~/.config/touchbar-strip/config.json
(re-read every 2 s): a built-in action name, "sh:<command>", or null. See README.md.

Python standard library plus pycairo and PyGObject (Pango).
  touchbar-strip --preview out.png   one frame, no hardware
  touchbar-strip --check             the configured actions and whether their helpers exist
"""
